loped and deployed robust RESTful APIs." You could also consider adding a brief description of the project\'s objectives and challenges to provide context and further showcase your skills.']}, {'title': 'Skills', 'description': 'Olusegun lists a good range of skills, including programming languages, frameworks and libraries, and tools and platforms. This section effectively showcases his technical expertise and demonstrates his ability to work with different technologies.', 'ats_match': '90%', 'recommendations': ['Consider organizing your skills into categories to make it easier for recruiters to quickly identify relevant skills. For example, you could have sections for "Programming Languages", "Frameworks and Libraries", and "Tools and Platforms". This will also make the section more visually appealing and improve readability.']}, {'title': 'Education', 'description': "Olusegun's educational background is clearly presented, highlighting his degree in Computer Science from Catholic University College, Ghana. This section demonstrates his academic foundation in the field.", 'ats_match': '80%', 'recommendations': ['Consider including any relevant coursework or projects that showcase your skills and experience. If you have any relevant certifications, include those as well.']}, {'title': 'Additional Tips', 'description': "Overall, Olusegun's resume is well-structured and presents a compelling case for his qualifications. However, there are a few minor improvements that could be made to enhance its impact.", 'ats_match': None, 'recommendations': ['Use a consistent font throughout your resume. Use a professional-looking font like Arial, Times New Roman, or Calibri. Ensure your resume is formatted consistently. Use clear headings, bullet points, and white space to make your resume easy to read. Proofread carefully for any typos or grammatical errors.  Keep your resume concise and to the point.  Avoid using jargon or technical terms that may not be understood by a general 